{
  "$comment": [
    "k6 function stress budgets. Every number here is a CLAIM this platform asserts, mirroring the",
    "philosophy of config/performance-budget.json: the first run produces the measurement, and these",
    "values are then revised to reality or the platform is tightened. A threshold nobody chose is not",
    "a threshold.",
    "",
    "The 'functions' array is the coverage contract: it enumerates the operator/user product surfaces",
    "the suite must exercise, per role, and the k6 script derives BOTH its traffic mix and its k6",
    "thresholds from this file. An endpoint missing here is a surface the stress suite does not cover,",
    "so adding a product surface means adding an entry here — enforced by",
    "test/k6-stress-suite.contract.spec.ts, which resolves every declared path back to a real controller.",
    "",
    "Every entry must be expected to answer 2xx for the declared role once the stress baseline is",
    "seeded; the setup stage fails the run when a required entity is absent, so 'no data' can never look",
    "like 'healthy under load'.",
    "",
    "Deliberately NOT covered (each listed in notStressed with its reason): long-lived SSE streams,",
    "machine-only surfaces (broker auth/ACL/webhooks, billing cycle/webhook, device",
    "pair/heartbeat/rotate), camera playback signalling (needs a live go2rtc), OTA campaign writes, and",
    "device-mutating public writes (`/v1` DEVICE_CONTROL) because a stress run must never act on real",
    "actuators."
  ],
  "schema": "iot-platform-k6-function-stress/1",
  "settings": {
    "executor": "ramping-arrival-rate",
    "startRate": 5,
    "preAllocatedVUs": 10,
    "maxVUs": 120,
    "timeUnit": "1s",
    "stages": [
      {
        "target": 10,
        "duration": "30s"
      },
      {
        "target": 40,
        "duration": "1m"
      },
      {
        "target": 80,
        "duration": "1m"
      },
      {
        "target": 0,
        "duration": "30s"
      }
    ],
    "gracefulStop": "30s",
    "scenarioName": "all_functions"
  },
  "thresholds": {
    "$comment": "Global gates on k6 built-in metrics; the suite additionally emits one trend per class so the class budgets below are enforced per surface rather than hidden behind an aggregate.",
    "http_req_failed": {
      "rate": 0.005
    },
    "http_req_duration": {
      "p95Ms": 1500
    },
    "checks": {
      "rate": 0.99
    },
    "classes": {
      "health": {
        "p95Ms": 250,
        "errorRate": 0.001
      },
      "read": {
        "p95Ms": 900,
        "errorRate": 0.002
      },
      "write": {
        "p95Ms": 2500,
        "errorRate": 0.01
      },
      "publicApi": {
        "p95Ms": 900,
        "errorRate": 0.002
      },
      "deviceProtocol": {
        "p95Ms": 600,
        "errorRate": 0.001
      }
    }
  },
